		<content type="html" xml:base="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/viewtopic.php?p=4367#p4367"><![CDATA[
From analysis of the problem, I found that objects don't precess ever if no torque is on them. In real life they do if they have different moments of inertia. Maby Euler's equations can help.<br><br>Newton game dynamics suffers from the same problem.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=1492">fast solve</a> — Thu May 31, 2007 3:19 am</p><hr />
]]></content>
